From e6656223679ec964217ef88f309ac095cf2ed2e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dnz3d4c <dnz3d4c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:29:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Korean: the 35 lines the generator cannot reach
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hand-written on purpose, and kept out of the generated commit. These are the
shapes tools/ko-apply does not parse - a ternary nested inside an interpolation,
a string built by concatenation, an array, a singular/plural branch. Mixing them
into the generated patch would lose them silently on the next regeneration, and
what would go missing is Korean, so the German/English snapshot would stay green
while the mod quietly went back to speaking English.

Every one of them adds a Korean arm in front and leaves the existing German and
English arms untouched, character for character. The snapshot proves it: 688
pairs unchanged.

Four of them are not translations.

- Korean has no plural, so the singular/plural branch collapses. ItemsCountLabel
  is one word now, and so are ForYourClasses, MateriaSlots, KeybindConflictsShort
  and CategorySummary
- The compass arrays stay TWO arrays even though the Korean words are identical
  in both. Merging them would force German and English to share one, and those
  two do differ (nördlich vs north)
- AttributeValue has German and English arms that are byte-identical. The Korean
  arm is real ("마이너스"/"플러스"), but the other two are still a branch with
  nothing in it - worth removing upstream
- HelpFull is 34 concatenated fragments per language. A dropped fragment still
  compiles and still sounds like a sentence, so the count was checked: 34, 34, 34

Game words come from the Korean client's Addon sheet, not from guesswork.
Materia is 마테리아 (Addon 481) - the project's own notes had written 머티리어,
which the game does not use anywhere.

Build: 0 warnings, 0 errors against ClientStructs 7.55 and 7.51
Verified: DE/EN snapshot unchanged - 688 pairs. HelpFull fragment count equal
across the three languages
In-Game: not checked

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
